            <ArticleTitle>Case report: ultrasonographic demonstration of portal vein thrombosis in the acute abdomen.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>101-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Ultrasonography demonstrated thrombus within the portal venous system in a child who presented with abdominal pain and a fever. This helped lead to a diagnosis of appendicitis complicated by ascending septic thrombophlebitis. Ultrasound of the portal vein may be of value when investigating such children with atyptical abdominal pain.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
